    coreField: "emotionalMeaning", coreAddition: "Fear may focus on injury, but betrayal becomes central when a trusted animal attacks. Anger during self-defense can show mobilization rather than helplessness, while freezing may reflect uncertainty about which response is safest. Escaping without injury can still leave vigilance or disbelief, especially when the threat appeared without warning. Protecting another person adds responsibility and fear that personal action may not be enough to keep someone safe."
